BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 72 740 Td (Sample paper generated by this app for testing. Not a real published article.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Peer Tutoring and Reading Habits of First-Year Students:) Tj T* (Evidence from Three Universities) Tj T* () Tj T* (An Example and Binh Sample) Tj T* (Journal of Demonstration Studies, Vol. 1, 2025 \(fictional journal\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Note: all names, institutions and data in this paper are fictional.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Abstract) Tj T* (This paper asks whether a weekly peer-tutoring program changes how much) Tj T* (first-year students read outside class. We followed 412 students at three) Tj T* (universities for one semester and compared tutored students with a matched) Tj T* (comparison group. Peer tutoring raised weekly reading time by about 2.1 hours.) Tj T* (The effect was larger for students who lived far from campus.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Keywords: peer tutoring, reading habits, first-year students) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 1) Tj T* ET
