BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 72 740 Td (Sample paper generated by this app for testing. Not a real published article.) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. Introduction) Tj T* (Many first-year students read little beyond assigned slides. Universities) Tj T* (often respond with extra lectures, but these add to an already full timetable.) Tj T* (Peer tutoring is cheaper and lets older students share how they plan their) Tj T* (reading. Earlier work has mostly looked at grades rather than reading time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2. Research question) Tj T* (Our main question is whether joining a weekly peer-tutoring group increases) Tj T* (the number of hours first-year students spend reading course materials.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3. Methods) Tj T* (We used a quasi-experimental design with propensity score matching and a) Tj T* (difference-in-differences model on reading diaries collected every week.) Tj T* (The sample covers 412 first-year students from three public universities) Tj T* (in the 2024 autumn semester; 206 joined tutoring groups and 206 did not.) Tj T* (Students recorded their reading time in a short online diary each Sunday.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 2) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
