BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 72 740 Td (Sample paper generated by this app for testing. Not a real published article.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4. Results) Tj T* (Before the program, both groups read about 3.4 hours per week. After twelve) Tj T* (weeks, tutored students read 5.6 hours per week while the comparison group) Tj T* (read 3.5 hours. Peer tutoring raised weekly reading time by about 2.1 hours.) Tj T* (The estimate stays between 1.8 and 2.4 hours across all robustness checks.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The effect was largest among students living more than 10 km from campus,) Tj T* (who gained 2.9 hours per week, compared with 1.6 hours for those living) Tj T* (on or near campus.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Tran et al. \(2021\) reported that a similar program raised library visits by) Tj T* (18 percent, which is in line with the direction of our findings.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 3) Tj T* ET
endstream
